// Creature figure bindings: which figure a creature presents. Each
// entry's present fields decide its key shape — monster alone keys by
// kind, race+class keys by vocation within a race, race alone keys the
// race default. Monsters resolve through their kind; humanoid
// creatures take the most specific matching key (race+class, then
// race). A race with no classless instances (people — always some
// class) needs no race default; every declared race and every declared
// monster must still be reachable by at least one entry, and an
// identity matching nothing fails at attach. The figure vocabulary and
// its render data live in the figure table; this file only binds.
[
    ( race: "human", class: "warrior", figure: "warrior" ),
    ( monster: "giant_white_rat", figure: "giant_white_rat" ),
]
